    "title": "Missing 45-year-old woman last seen at Norman sporting goods store found dead - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mario Gonzalez/KFOR ,\n7 hours ago\nNORMAN, Okla. ( KFOR ) — Police confirm that a 45-year-old woman who was reported missing on Monday morning in Norman has been found dead.\nThe Norman Police Department released an alert on Monday, seeking the community's help in locating Melanie Garcia after she was last seen at Academy Sports & Outdoors at around 9:30 a.m. that day.\nPREVIOUS REPORTING: Norman Police looking for missing woman last seen at sporting goods store According to investigators at the time, Garcia's recent behavior was abnormal, and she could have been a danger to herself.\nOn Wednesday, the department provided an update, saying that she was found dead; however, her death was not believed to be suspicious.\nOfficials have not released any further information regarding her death or where she was found.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KFOR.com Oklahoma City.\n21",
    "summary": "The Norman Police Department released an alert on Monday, seeking the community's help in locating Melanie Garcia after she was last seen at Academy Sports & Outdoors at around 9:30 a.m. that day. PREVIOUS REPORTING: Norman Police looking for missing woman last seen at sporting goods store According to investigators at the time, Garcia's recent behavior was abnormal, and she could have been a danger to herself. On Wednesday, the department provided an update, saying that she was found dead; however, her death was not believed to be suspicious. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.",
